<<~ ahu slot=`#/pronaos-scout-lares-pronaos-lararium-architectur`>>

! Pronaos-Scout: Lares (Tasked Spirit) — pronaos + lararium architecture, memory-stage scout (2026-10-31)

Read-only. Grounds: canon read whole (pronaos.mem, pronaos-carriers.mem), road sections by grep, session-contract #/the-hands, wiki-layer-ontology (daemon wiki), code read at the cited lines. TESTIMONY marks what I inferred without running. Nothing booted.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/1-what-pronaos-is`>>

!! 1. What pronaos is

Pronaos = a lararium's own "first face": the arrival page, the arrival descriptor (`/.well-known/lar`), `/genesis/seed.json`, seed-named CAS members. "Only a lararium lights a Pronaos" (pronaos.mem #/the-placement); a herm may only carry bytes by CID (mirror) or post an unsigned waymark. Status line in the carrier reads PROPOSED, yet #/the-first-arrival marks the node adapter BUILT (`pronaos-adapter.ts`, `pronaos-composition.ts`). It holds public delivery only: no persona, no document, no VEIL read, no admission. Five relations never grant one another: name, secure origin, peer key, route, capability.

Canon vocabulary: "anon floor" appears as the lease/veil floor (lararium-identity) and as the "waking floor" (waking-floor.mem): every boot rests at the floor until a human unlocks; the floor still serves the arrival page.

```
 name / LAN / QR
   -> Compitum (roads meet)
   -> HERM floor (every vessel; carriage, CID bulb, optional waymark)   <- anon floor, faceless place
   -> PRONAOS (lararium only: / , /assets, /genesis/*, /.well-known/lar) <- served by the NODE http server
   -> LARARIUM inner house (face/persona, bags, working layers, custody)  <- opens only after unlock + face

 node (root holder)                              browser (leaf)
  place founded (faceless, floor)                  page from node origin (or Vite dev)
  found --hearth: place + persona 0 + charter      browser vessel at floor: IDB identity, NO face
  daemon @ ws://:port/ws, UDS rendezvous           passphrase slot (B1) -> fleet-join request
  vault unlock -> face lit                         paste answer -> land -> reboot on admit
         \__ fleet join: offer (node) -> request (browser) -> answer (node) -> land (browser) __/
                       one face, two vessels, sync over relay ws
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/2-full-rite-sequence-canon-vs-code`>>

!! 2. Full rite sequence, canon vs code

Canon carriers: road #/Steps item 4 (human route on a TTY; test door), #/rulings (A face's secrets never rest clear; browser leaf holds a slot first), session-contract, waking-floor, pronaos #/first-arrival. Cmd map in `packages/lares-cli/src/commands/vessel.ts:100-210`.

| # | Step | Command / UI act | Canon | Code today | Harness drives? |h
| 0 | scratch root | `export LAR_ROOT=~/.lares-scratch/<lane>/root`; `genesis/` must exist under it (or `LAR_GENESIS`) | road Steps 1 | env only; no copier (gap G6) | yes |
| 1 | build | `pnpm -r build`, `build:tw5-vendor`, `stamp-build`; web build writes `.pronaos-build/pronaos-artifact.json` (`lararium-web/vite.config.ts:8`) | road Steps 3 | exists | yes |
| 2 | found place | `lares vessel found` (faceless place, mints vessel key, custody from birth) | founding; `found.ts:105-111` | TTY route (`custody-prompt.ts`) | operator on TTY; harness: `tools/test-scratch-marker.mjs`, `tools/seed-test-custody.mjs`, `found --skip-build` |
| 2b | or hearth founding | `found --hearth --name <label>`: place + persona 0 + one-seat seed charter + face (`found.ts:17`, `found-hearth.ts:194`). Alternatively `persona new 0 --name` lights the face (`persona.ts` personaNew, `init.ts:514`) | stable founding act | exists | same as 2 |
| 3 | stand | `lares vessel stand` (daemon detached, `stand.ts:254`: `node dist/src/main.js --port --root`) | every boot at floor | exists; needs `LAR_SAME_ORIGIN=true` and `LAR_PRONAOS_WEB_ROOT`+`LAR_PRONAOS_ARTIFACT_RECORD` to serve a page; stand passes none | yes |
| 4 | unlock | `lares vault unlock` (custody frame; `vault.ts:209`) | waking-floor; "node unlocks once per boot" (road :201) | exists | operator TTY; harness `tools/unlock-test-custody.mjs` on marked scratch root |
| 5 | seed corpus | `lares vessel seed` (`vessel.ts:127`) | founding rite = found · stand · seed | exists | yes |
| 6 | page arrives | open the node origin | pronaos #/first-arrival, #/declared-path | built, but only if step 3 envs set (`pronaos-composition.ts:110-140`, `main.ts:291`); otherwise 404 at `/` with a boot notice (`pronaosShoreBootNotice`, :96) | yes |
| 7 | browser at floor | page boots a browser vessel: IDB identity, no face. Dials a relay only with `?relay=ws://…` (`lararium-web/src/main.ts:365`, `live-status.ts:45`); with none it says "PURE LOCAL BOOT" and prints `not pinned · ws://host/ws` (:556) | rungs 0-1, road :417 | built | harness via Playwright |
| 8 | browser slot | passphrase/paper slot form (`main.ts:116-139`) before any face secret (`B1`) | #/rulings, road :199-200 | built | UI act; operator types passphrase (a test could, TESTIMONY: not measured) |
| 9 | offer | node: `lares fleet join offer --out offer.json` (`fleet.ts:81`) | face-proof chain; "fleet join serves every face" | built | needs unlocked face; operator hand (custody) |
| 10 | request | browser: paste offer (`main.ts:299-319`, `browserFleetJoinRequest`) | browser-fleet-join.ts header | built | UI act |
| 11 | answer | node: `lares fleet join answer <request> --out answer.json` (`fleet.ts:94-98`) | same | built | operator hand |
| 12 | land | browser: paste answer; `browserFleetJoinLand` then re-boot on admit (`main.ts:221`) | same | built | UI act |
| 13 | settle | `browserFleetJoinSettle` after boot stands | same | built | auto |

Agents may only drive 0-3, 5, 6, 7 through the test door; 2, 4, 8, 9, 11 are the operator's hand under the road (:66 "the operator performs each founding and custody act"). Gate 4 interacts: after 2-3 a harness reads `gate key:` from the log.

