<<~ ahu slot=`#/4-daemon-wiki-as-memory-stage`>>

!! 4. Daemon wiki as memory-stage

Canon already says it: wiki-layer-ontology "The daemon wiki" ahu: <code>&#64;daemon</code> HOLDS THE WORKING-MEMORY STAGE, "the one place work crosses between hands must land on disk to read, diff or commit." Its working layer projects to `<LAR_ROOT>/wikis/daemon/` (`bag-paths.ts:132-138`; `open-daemon-vm.ts:82`, `node-daemon-island.ts:68`); the daemon bag beneath (`bags/daemon`) is control plane and stays unmirrored. So: design tracking = tiddlers/memes in the daemon wiki's working layer, addressed `lar:` URIs.

Door: `lares meme put|get|list|delete|project <uri> --recipe default [--base <hash>]` (`meme.ts` header :4-41; `--recipe default` = the daemon's own wiki). MCP twin in `packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts/lares_mcp.py` (1309 lines, read): tools `meme_put/get/list/delete/project` (lines 885-960) take exactly one of `recipe`/`bag` (container law), ride `lares_uds.call` over the UDS rendezvous derived from `LAR_ROOT` (`lares_uds.py:46-81`), `requestedBy` = the vessel's verifying key by designation (:100-113), no Mask, no profile. Also exposed: pour/sweep/recall/status/worldline/kapae/un_kapae/rejim/analyze/ki/li/jing/couple_r/forecast/mismatch/flow/plane_record (sensorium; the mempalace line is BURNED per memory, so these may refuse), `wiki` switcher, and sense lifecycle (roster..purge). `DaemonCoordinator` holds no store; `main()` refuses with no daemon socket. To bind a scratch vessel the MCP entry needs `env: {LAR_ROOT: ...}`.

Law for an AI writing there: session-contract #/the-hands. A spirit holds a seat, not a key; its writes land in the working layer and reach a bag only by a person's residency move; a standing seat drafts and never signs authority changes (vault, admit, kapae, face switch, residency move into a bag). Wikis-first writes (operator 2026-09-13, memory `project_projection_is_a_deliberate_act`): `wikis/*/working` is the AI surface; `bags/` by promotion only. TWO UNBUILT PARTS, measured: (1) `meme promote` holds admin false (`meme.ts:1109`, `holdsAdmin: async () => false`), so canon promotion is gated; (2) the profile gate and Mask are owed (`F11`, session-contract "OWED": a watcher or tab session runs face rows as its face; the MCP seat has no standing-grant mount). Memory file `project_projection_is_a_deliberate_act` says `wikis/` never produced a file; still true here (`git ls-files wikis` = 0, dir absent): the memory is current.

Landing in git: `.gitignore` ignores only `wikis/scratch/`; a scratch `LAR_ROOT` keeps `wikis/daemon/` outside the repo, so git landing = the operator copying/promoting the projected files (no verb does it). That fits "operator-triggered at first".

Custody: writes need an unlocked face; MCP "opens nothing while the vessel rests at the floor" (session-contract). A floor vessel runs only faceless-floor verbs (TESTIMONY on whether `meme put --recipe default` clears at the floor: `open-daemon-vm` floor verifier admits "a verb the vessel's own presence channel took" on a bag it registered; the daemon wiki is that bag, so likely yes; verify).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/5-smallest-ordered-build-rows`>>

!! 5. Smallest ordered build rows (red-first, none touches custody)

Order: R1 -> R2 -> R3 -> R4 -> R5. R1-R3 are small disjoint-file lane work.

| Row | Size | Files | Merges/reorders | Red-first shape |h
| R1 stand serves the page | S | `lares-cli/src/commands/stand.ts:254` (env), `pronaos-composition.ts` | New row beside `FW`; independent | Red: stage a scratch root with built dist+record, `stand`, `GET /` must be 200 `text/html`; today 404 + `NO PRONAOS SHORE` notice. Control: no built web -> notice stays. Env derived only when both files exist; `LAR_SAME_ORIGIN` declared by `stand --with-page` flag. |
| R2 same-origin default relay | S | `lararium-web/src/live-status.ts:45`, `main.ts:365,556` | Closes rung-1 to rung-2 gap; precedes FW/W5 | Red: page served by node with no `?relay=` must dial `sameOriginRelayUrl`; today logs PURE LOCAL BOOT. Control: opened from file:// or Vite keeps local boot. |
| R3 MCP seat bind | S | `lararium-mempalace/src/spawn-resolve`, `mcp-resolve.ts`, `lares home tend` MCP wire; `requirements` check | Rides `F11` (seat) and the surface-parity witness | Red: `resolveLaresMcp()` for a scratch `LAR_ROOT` returns env with `LAR_ROOT`, and an import probe of `mcp.server.mcpserver` fails by name when the venv holds mcp&lt;2.3 (today a silent "Connection closed"). Then `meme_put recipe=default` + `lares meme get` read the same bytes. |
| R4 stage walk (the loop) | M | `tools/browser-weld/` new walk, `tools/browser-ci.sh`; join step by operator-hand or test door | IS `FW`/W5/W7 (:609); needs `ONE FACE` working layer for rung 2's node half | Red: joined browser edits a tiddler in `daemon` wiki -> file appears at `<LAR_ROOT>/wikis/daemon/...mem` and `lares meme get --recipe default` returns it, and a CLI `meme put` shows in the page. Weaken: kill relay -> no file. |
| R5 spirit seat profile + Mask | M | `uds-session-door.ts`, `lares_uds.py`, session profile table | IS `F11` | Red: an MCP-seat session calling a vault/admit/face-switch verb must refuse by profile; `meme_put` carries a Mask field. Needed before agents write outside scratch. |
| (R6, later) promotion verb | M | `meme.ts:1109`, `meme-promote.ts` | Wikis-first writes row (road :611), lands last | Red: `meme promote` of a working-layer meme by an operator with admin moves it into a bag as a residency move with an unchanged `lar:` URI. |

Smallest set that closes the stated loop: R1, R2, R3, R4. Everything above in 2 that needs a human hand (2, 4, 8, 9, 11) stays the operator's; the loop's harness half uses the test door.

